+// carried out now; Internal gets the status and InternalHigh the bytes
+// moved, and hEvent (if any) is set. On a handle opened with
+// FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED and associated with a completion port, the call
+// returns FALSE with ERROR_IO_PENDING and the completion arrives as a
+// packet (key, bytes, the OVERLAPPED), unless hEvent's low bit asks for no
+// packet; otherwise it completes synchronously (TRUE, and a synchronous
+// handle's file pointer moves past the transfer). A read at or past the
+// end of the file fails with ERROR_HANDLE_EOF and queues nothing.
